# codetracer-desktop capabilities file.  The line format and the routing
# rules for every keyword below are specified in CodeTracer-Launcher.md
# §2.3; installers copy this file to
# <components-root>/codetracer-desktop@<version>/capabilities
# (codetracer-launcher/src/install.nim).  Human-readable help TEXT is not
# here -- it comes from `ct ct-describe-commands` at runtime.
#
# SIZE BUDGET -- READ THIS BEFORE ADDING ANYTHING.  The launcher parses
# this file into a fixed 4096-byte CapBuffer
# (codetracer-launcher/src/caps.nim) and `just test-desktop-component`
# FAILS the build when the file exceeds it.  A declaration costs its own
# length; a paragraph of prose costs hundreds of bytes.  Explanations
# longer than a couple of lines belong in
# codetracer-specs/Testing/Launcher-Recorder-Compatibility-Tests.md §5.1,
# not here.
#
# THE EXTENSION LISTS ARE DERIVED, NOT FREE-FORM.  Every extension below
# has a real dispatch path in this repo, and every extension the core can
# dispatch is listed.  `just test-desktop-capabilities` recomputes both
# sets from src/ct/utilities/language_detection.nim's LANGS table plus
# src/ct/trace/recorder_dispatch.nim and fails on any difference, so do
# not edit an extension here without changing those tables.
#
# EVERY COMMAND `ct-describe-commands` ADVERTISES MUST BE DECLARED HERE.
# One that is not is listed on `ct --help` and then refused by the router
# -- which is how `ct review` shipped broken.  The bare lines carry no
# extension list on purpose: `caps.matches` yields mkNone for a dot-less
# argument, so `ct review collect`, `ct doctor` and `ct trace export` need
# an unqualified declaration.
#
# NO `project` MARKERS ARE DECLARED, DELIBERATELY.  The launcher DROPS an
# unqualified command match when a component declares markers and none of
# them match the cwd (codetracer-launcher/src/launcher.nim,
# `projectMarkerOutcome` == 1 -> `continue`), so markers here would stop
# `ct replay <id>`, `ct list`, `ct login`, ... routing outside a marked
# directory; and the core has no cwd-driven project record path to justify
# them anyway.  Full reasoning: design §5.1 D2 (milestone LRC-1).
#
# All three rules above are enforced by
# ci/test/desktop-capabilities-dispatch.sh, in both directions.

name codetracer-desktop
bin codetracer
description CodeTracer desktop application -- launcher help delegate
help-delegate

# KNOWN GAP: `.ex` `.exs` `.erl` `.hrl` ROUTE but do not RECORD.
#   `ct record foo.ex` exits 0 with a recordingId and a 2-event, 0-function
#   trace: recorder_dispatch.nim sends `-- elixir <prog>`, which
#   codetracer-beam-recorder's is_beam_target() rejects. Full diagnosis in
#   codetracer-beam-recorder/cross-repo/launcher-compat.yml. Revisit these
#   four extensions when it is fixed.
# `noext` and `known-extensions` are routing tokens, not file types.  Rule and
# rationale: codetracer-specs/Planned-Features/Native-Target-Recognition.md §4.
record .py .rb .js .mjs .ts .php .ex .exs .erl .hrl .sh .bash .zsh .nim .nims .nr .wasm .sol .masm .sw .move .cairo .circom .leo .tolk .ak .cdc noext
record-test .py
run .py .rb .js .mjs .ts .php .ex .exs .erl .hrl .sh .bash .zsh .nim .nims .nr .wasm .sol .masm .sw .move .cairo .circom .leo .tolk .ak .cdc noext
# `.gd` is KNOWN, not recorded: the core refuses GDScript by name (its patched
# Godot engine is unpublished).  On `record` it would advertise a missing tool.
known-extensions .c .cpp .rs .go .pas .f90 .d .cr .lean .adb .gd
replay
list
print
install
host
upload
download
login
edit
review
import
ci
help
remote
activate
check-license
build
console
arb
index-diff
set-default-org
get-default-org
trace
gfx-replay
doctor
